    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia successfully received funding from the Green Climate Fund (GCF) under its REDD+ Results-Based Payment (RBP) pilot program for 20.25 million tco2eq of emission reductions achieved from deforestation under its REDD+ program for the period 2014 to 2016 through the implementation of the National REDD+ Strategy (STRANAS).</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The implementation of REDD+ enabling activities in Indonesia continues accelerating the achievement of Output 2. the PBPA signed and the first disbursement of Output 2 transferred.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Through REDD+ RBP Project, UNDP support the GoI in compiling and finalizing 2 important ministerial regulations: 1) Ministerial Regulation of the Ministry of Environment and Forestry No. 21/2022 on the Procedures for Implementing the Carbon Economic Value and the Ministerial Regulation No. 10/2022 on the Preparation of a General Plan for Forest and Land Rehabilitation of Watersheds and Annual Plan for Forest and Land Rehabilitation. The first one is important as it will be the basis of Rumah Karbon, carbon trading, and NDC. It will also regulate the type of emission reduction activities outside NDC that can be traded. The second regulation is no less important as all of the forest and land rehabilitation activities will be based in the MoEF and UNDP assisted the preparation of the regulation. 
2. UNDP support the GoI in improving the National Strategy Document (Stranas). The latest document in 2022 will set the direction for the sustainable forest management programmes 2021 - 2030. Currently the document is being finalized and will be uploaded in the first quarter 2023.
3. REDD+ RBP project also improved and assisted the development of the National Registration System (SRN). SRN has been applied as the integrated system of the overall mitigation activities (on emission reduction) and adaptation activities (increased resilience). The project integrated the achievement of emission reduction and SIS (safeguard information system) of REDD+.
4. UNDP has been facilitated the payment of the non-reimbursable fund from GCF to the Indonesian Environment Fund (IEF) by using UNDPs Performance Based Payment (PBP) modality. In December, GoI will receive USD 47 Million for its stewardship in climate action and conservation following the success in its forest protection and conservation in the 2014 - 2016. The 47 million USD marks the first disbursement of the Indonesias Result-based payment for REDD+ project which will be a total of USD 103 million from the GCF. Parts of the funds will go towards the implementation of Indonesias Social Forestry Programme which aims to alleviate poverty, halt deforestation, and end forestland conflict by empowering local communities to manage forests themselves. All of the activities will contribute to the countrys FOLU Net Sink 2030 which is a pivotal component of the countrys enhanced NDC.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
